      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>ab-</b> (also <b>abs-</b>) = <b>away, from</b>. <b>ad-</b> = <b>to, toward</b>. <b>pro-</b> = <b>forward, forth</b>, and sometimes <b>for</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "<b>ad-</b> is a master of disguise. It changes its <i>d</i> to match the next letter: <i>accede</i>, <i>affable</i>, <i>aggregate</i>, <i>alleviate</i>, <i>annihilate</i>, <i>apprehensive</i>, <i>arrogant</i>, <i>assert</i>. A doubled letter after a first <i>a</i> is the clue."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
