      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>abstain</b><br>to choose not to do or have something",
            "<b>abs-</b> <i>away</i> + tain <i>hold</i><br>→ “hold away from”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>absolve</b><br>to free from guilt or blame",
            "<b>ab-</b> <i>from</i> + solv <i>loosen</i> + -e<br>→ “loosen from (set free)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>aberration</b><br>a departure from what is normal or right",
            "<b>ab-</b> <i>away</i> + err <i>wander</i> + -ation<br>→ “a wandering away”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>adversary</b><br>an opponent",
            "<b>ad-</b> <i>toward</i> + vers <i>turn</i> + -ary<br>→ “one turned toward you (against you)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>alleviate</b><br>to make pain or trouble easier to bear",
            "<b>al-</b> <i>to</i> + lev <i>light</i> + -iate<br>→ “make light”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>affluent</b><br>wealthy",
            "<b>af-</b> <i>to</i> + flu <i>flow</i> + -ent<br>→ “flowing to (riches flowing in)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>accede</b><br>to agree to a request or demand",
            "<b>ac-</b> <i>to</i> + ced <i>go, yield</i><br>→ “yield to”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>procrastinate</b><br>to delay doing something one should do",
            "<b>pro-</b> <i>forward</i> + crastin <i>of tomorrow</i> + -ate<br>→ “put forward to tomorrow”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>propensity</b><br>a natural tendency to behave a certain way",
            "<b>pro-</b> <i>forward</i> + pens <i>hang</i> + -ity<br>→ “a hanging forward (a leaning)”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "Dev always <b>procrastinates</b>: his report is due tomorrow and he has not started. What does <i>procrastinate</i> mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>pro-</b> (forward) + <b>crastin</b> (of tomorrow, from Latin <i>cras</i>, tomorrow) + <b>-ate</b>.",
          "Literally: “to put forward to tomorrow.”",
          "The sentence fits: he keeps pushing the work to the next day."
        ],
        "a": "To delay doing something one should do."
      },
